        "original_id": "9c89e2de-f986-55a4-a1ab-8dd10d04402a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pepper Keenan, Rob Parissi\n- Bands: Corrosion of Conformity, Down, Wild Cherry\n- Songs: Play That Funky Music\n- Places: Mingo Junction, Ohio\n\nFacts:\n- Rob Parissi was born in 1950 and was raised in the steel mill town of Mingo Junction, Ohio.\n- In 1976, Wild Cherry had the chart-topping song \"Play That Funky Music,\" which Rob Parissi wrote.\n- Pepper J. Keenan was born on May 8, 1967.\n- Pepper J. Keenan is an American guitarist and vocalist best known for his work with the heavy metal bands Corrosion of Conformity and Down.\n- Rob Parissi is an American singer, songwriter, and guitarist who is best known as the frontman of the American funk group Wild Cherry.",
